MoinMoin 1.12.0 (moinmoin-py3-md) - notes for Debian, Devuan and derivatives
============================================================================

This package contains MoinMoin 1.12.0 (moinmoin-py3-md): MoinMoin 1.9.11
ported to Python 3, with support for pages written in Markdown next to
the pages in MoinMoin wiki syntax. It does not
need systemd: on Devuan the wikis run with sysvinit/OpenRC (init script
/etc/init.d/moinmoin) or inside any web server.

Files
-----

 /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/MoinMoin   the wiki engine
 /usr/bin/moin                             command line tool (accounts, maintenance, server)
 /usr/sbin/moin-mkwiki                     creates a new wiki instance
 /usr/share/moin/                          templates: config, data, underlay, server scripts
 /usr/share/moin/htdocs                    static files (alias /moin_static1120)
 /etc/default/moinmoin, /etc/init.d/moinmoin   standalone servers (disabled by default)
 /usr/share/doc/moinmoin-py3-md/examples/ Apache, nginx, uWSGI, lighttpd, systemd examples

Creating a wiki
---------------

  moin-mkwiki -n "My Wiki" -s AdminUser /srv/moin/mywiki
  moin --config-dir=/srv/moin/mywiki --wiki-url=http://localhost/ \
       account create --name=AdminUser --email=admin@example.org --password=...

Log in as AdminUser and install the help and system pages from the page
LanguageSetup (e.g. "English--all_pages.zip"). The pages appear after
the wiki is restarted (this is the same with the original MoinMoin).

Running the wiki
----------------

 * Standalone server (simplest, also behind a reverse proxy):
   set INSTANCES in /etc/default/moinmoin, then
     /etc/init.d/moinmoin start      (Devuan: service moinmoin start)
   update-rc.d already enabled the script at boot; it does nothing while
   INSTANCES is empty.

 * Apache + mod_wsgi:  apt install libapache2-mod-wsgi-py3
   examples/apache-mod_wsgi.conf

 * nginx + uWSGI:      apt install uwsgi uwsgi-plugin-python3 nginx
   examples/uwsgi-mywiki.ini, examples/nginx-uwsgi.conf

 * gunicorn:           apt install gunicorn
   cp /srv/moin/mywiki/moin.wsgi /srv/moin/mywiki/moin_wsgi.py
   gunicorn -b 127.0.0.1:8080 --chdir /srv/moin/mywiki moin_wsgi:application
   and examples/nginx-proxy.conf

 * CGI / FastCGI / SCGI: the scripts moin.cgi, moin.fcgi, moin.scgi of the
   instance, examples/apache-cgi.conf, apache-fcgid.conf, lighttpd-fastcgi.conf

The data directory must be writable by the user running the wiki
(www-data by default, see moin-mkwiki -u/-g).

Markdown pages
--------------

The markup of a page without a #format line is recognized from its text
(markup_autodetect = True, the default); pages that are not clearly
Markdown use default_markup (MoinMoin wiki syntax by default). The markup
can always be set with a first line

  #format markdown        (or "#format moin" for MoinMoin wiki syntax)
 Markdown and wiki syntax pages can be mixed freely. The
help page HelpOnMarkdown (Italian: AiutoSuMarkdown) describes the syntax,
the page MarkdownTemplate is a template for new Markdown pages. The
Python-Markdown extensions can be chosen with markdown_extensions in
wikiconfig.py. Raw HTML in Markdown pages is never rendered.

Migrating a wiki from MoinMoin 1.9.x on Python 2
------------------------------------------------

The data format did not change: copy data/ (and underlay/ if it was
modified) of the old wiki into the instance, keep your wikiconfig.py
(check it with Python 3: e.g. no "print x" statements, string literals
are already unicode), then remove the old caches:

  moin --config-dir=/srv/moin/mywiki --wiki-url=http://localhost/ maint cleancache

Old cache files written by Python 2 are ignored anyway and recreated.
Third party plugins (data/plugin/*) must be ported to Python 3.

Security notes
--------------

 * Limits for the data sent to the wiki (since 1.11.0+md3), in wikiconfig.py:
     max_form_memory_size = 16 * 1024 * 1024  # form fields kept in memory
     max_form_parts = 1000                    # parts of a multipart request
     max_content_length = None                # whole request (attachments)
   Bigger requests get "413 Request Entity Too Large". A limit for the whole
   request can also be set in the web server (Apache LimitRequestBody,
   nginx client_max_body_size).
 * The session cookie is "httponly" (cookie_httponly = True, the default
   since 1.11.0+md3): scripts in the browser cannot read it.
 * The standalone server (moin ... server standalone, /etc/init.d/moinmoin)
   is the Werkzeug development server: it listens on 127.0.0.1 by default.
   Do not expose it directly to the Internet: put a web server in front
   of it (nginx-proxy.conf) or use Apache mod_wsgi / uWSGI. Never enable
   debug='web' on a public wiki.
 * By default only "Trusted" users may edit (acl_rights_default). The
   wikis created with moin-mkwiki have a random "secrets" value.

Not supported
-------------

 * the Jabber/XMPP notification bot (needs pyxmpp, which only exists for
   Python 2);
 * the DocBook and XSLT parsers (need 4Suite, Python 2 only);
 * the OpenID support has not been tested;
 * xapian indexed search needs python3-xapian (optional).

Running the test suite (source package)
---------------------------------------

  python3 -m pytest MoinMoin

Project home: https://github.com/asbestomolesto/moinmoin-py3-md

Credits
-------

MoinMoin was written by Juergen Hermann, Thomas Waldmann and the MoinMoin
developers. Version 1.10.0 (the Python 3 port) and this package were made by
Gabriele 'asbesto' Zaverio with the assistance of Claude (Anthropic AI): the
files written or modified by Claude carry a comment saying so at their top.

The maintainer does not have particular skills in Python and made this
project with Claude, so issues and security problems may be beyond what
the maintainer can understand or fix alone; the maintainer will do their
best, using AI to help.
Anyone more skilled is welcome to fork and maintain this project.
